# Publish / push (mandatory)

Canonical docs: [`docs/publish-runbook.md`](docs/publish-runbook.md), [`docs/agent-github-factory-publish.md`](docs/agent-github-factory-publish.md). Badges: [`.cursor/rules/green-badges.mdc`](green-badges.mdc).

## Order

1. **Commit** (stage only intended files — never `git add -A`; leave `lottery/alien-monitor`, warden scan memory alone).
2. **Gitea** (full monorepo, both servers): `./scripts/push_gitea_monorepo.sh`
3. **GitHub** (trimmed factory and/or satellites) via publish scripts only.

## Never

- `git push gh`, `git push origin` (or any plain `git push`) to **GitHub** for this monorepo / factory.
- Factory publish **without** `AICOM_FACTORY_REMOTE=https://github.com/alexar76/aicom.git` (guard aborts; do not work around it).
- Pointing `publish_aicom_factory.sh` / `--factory-only` at Gitea `origin` (would wipe canon).
- Pushing the **full** monorepo (with satellites) to `alexar76/aicom`.

## GitHub factory

```bash
GH_PAT=<token> \
AICOM_FACTORY_REMOTE=https://github.com/alexar76/aicom.git \
./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh --factory-only
# or: ./scripts/publish_aicom_factory.sh --message "…"
```

Auth: `GH_PAT` / `GITHUB_TOKEN` for **alexar76** (not `alexart2025` gh-cli session alone).

## GitHub satellite

```bash
GH_PAT=<token> ./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh --satellite <id>
# or: ./scripts/mirror_satellites.sh --satellite <id>
```

## Mental model

| Path | Script | Target |
|------|--------|--------|
| Full monorepo | `push_gitea_monorepo.sh` | Gitea only |
| Trimmed `aicom` | `publish_aicom_factory.sh` / `--factory-only` | `github.com/alexar76/aicom` |
| One satellite | `mirror_satellites.sh` / `--satellite` | that GitHub repo |
